Here are the Postman/curl commands to test Wikipedia API directly:

Test 1: Wikipedia Summary API

curl -X GET "https://en.wikipedia.org/api/rest_v1/page/summary/Elon_Musk" \
  -H "Accept: application/json" \
  -H "User-Agent: Mozilla/5.0"


Test 2: Wikipedia Search API

curl -X GET "https://en.wikipedia.org/w/api.php?action=query&list=search&srsearch=Elon+Musk&srlimit=3&format=json&origin=*" \
  -H "Accept: application/json"


Test 3: Wikipedia Page Extract (Full Summary)

curl -X GET "https://en.wikipedia.org/w/api.php?action=query&prop=extracts&exintro=true&explaintext=true&titles=Elon_Musk&format=json&origin=*" \
  -H "Accept: application/json"


Postman Setup
For Test 1:

Method: GET
URL: https://en.wikipedia.org/api/rest_v1/page/summary/Elon_Musk
Headers:
  Accept: application/json
  User-Agent: Mozilla/5.0


For Test 2:

Method: GET
URL: https://en.wikipedia.org/w/api.php
Params:
  action: query
  list: search
  srsearch: Elon Musk
  srlimit: 3
  format: json
  origin: *


Test these first and let me know which one returns a successful response — then we’ll use that exact endpoint inside Dify!​​​​​​​​​​​​​​​​
